      "body": "pillar_elongation → porosity"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[negative] replace BDC pillars with bulkier substituted BDC pillars such as NH2-BDC, Br-BDC, or NO2-BDC → surface area decreases along 2-BDC → 3-NH2-BDC → 5-Br-BDC → 4-NO2-BDC"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] vary the dicarboxylate pillars in pillar-layered MOFs → enables control and adjustment of pore size, pore shape, and functionality while preserving the layer structural motif"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "compound 2 with BDC ligand vs other metal-triazolate-dicarboxylate pillar-layered MOFs, most decorated with amino groups: winner=subject_a on CO2_uptake"
    },
    {
      "title": "Failure",
      "body": "[performance_regression] decorate metal-triazolate-dicarboxylate pillar-layered MOFs with amino groups to obtain the highest CO2 uptake: amino functionalization did not deliver the top CO2 uptake because compound 2 with a BDC ligand outperformed most amino-decorated analogues"
    }
